1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:01,600
I'm your China Travel Expert.
我是你的中国旅游专家

2
00:00:01,600 --> 00:00:04,000
One cocoon holds one unbroken thread.
一颗蚕茧，一根不断的丝

3
00:00:04,000 --> 00:00:06,400
Up to 900 meters — from a single cocoon.
长达900米，只出自一茧

4
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:08,800
China guarded this secret 1,000 years.
中国守了这秘密上千年

5
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,200
Smuggling a silkworm meant death.
私运蚕种，处死

6
00:00:11,200 --> 00:00:13,600
Monks hid eggs in hollow canes, 550 AD.
僧人把蚕卵藏进空竹杖

7
00:00:13,600 --> 00:00:16,000
This one thread named the Silk Road.
这一根丝，命名了丝绸之路

8
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:18,400
Double-tap if you'd wear this history.
想穿上这段历史，点个赞

9
00:00:18,400 --> 00:00:20,800
Sericulture — UNESCO heritage since 2009.
蚕桑丝织，2009年入非遗

10
00:00:20,800 --> 00:00:24,000
★ Expert Tip: Burn a thread — real silk smells like burnt hair, crushes to ash.
烧一根线：真丝有烧发味、成灰；假的熔成硬珠

11
00:00:24,000 --> 00:00:27,000
Silk or jade — which would you bring home?
丝绸还是玉，你带哪个回家
